cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Restora or build on it, please cite it as below."
title: "Restora: self-healing API tests from a spreadsheet"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vedant
    family-names: Surve
abstract: >-
  Restora runs API tests from a spreadsheet, a Postman collection or cURL
  commands. It fills gaps from earlier responses or realistic test data, orders
  rows so producers run before consumers, heals requests the API rejects by
  reading the error (rules first, an optional local AI model second), refuses to
  make negative tests pass or to heal server errors, and writes a corrected sheet
  with every change tracked.
repository-code: "https://github.com/VYADDISURVE07/restora"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-24
keywords:
  - API testing
  - test automation
  - self-healing tests
  - local LLM
  - pytest
